nent | Owner team (from architecture context) | Classification |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | **Active** — report views, data sourcing, CSV export |\n| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Workbenches | **Passive** — already tracks last-activity timestamps; no code changes (\"the data exists\") |\n| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | **Passive** — already retains run completion metadata; no code changes |\n| (HLR-4 documentation) | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | Active — substantive docs authoring |\n\nComponent name mappings (`.context/rhai-components.txt`): \"RHOAI web console\"\n→ `Dashboard`; \"Notebook controller\" → `Notebooks`; \"Kubeflow Pipelines\" →\n`Data Science Pipelines`. All three plus `Documentation` are canonical names.\n\n**Passive-component handling:** the strategy's premise is that the notebook\ncontroller and Kubeflow Pipelines already hold the needed data and need no\nchanges — only the console surfaces it. Validation that the reports correctly\nreflect each passive component's data therefore becomes acceptance criteria on\nthe nearest active component's epic (E001), not separate epics. The\ndifferent-team exception does not fire: no team involvement is stated in the\nstrategy, and the validation is a data-reconciliation check performed by the\nconsole team, not a sign-off owned by the Workbenches or RHOAI Pipelines\nteams.\n\n**New component detection:** all three code components have\narchitecture-context files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`,\n`notebooks.md`, `data-science-pipelines.md`) — all in-platform, all Konflux\nonboarded. No onboarding chain is needed. `Documentation` has no\narchitecture-context file, but it is a work-product component routed through\nthe Red Hat docs content process (`docs-authoring`), not a platform component\nto provision — no repo/konflux onboarding applies to it.\n\n## Step 3 — Investigation Epics\n\