eclamation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9016-E001: Idle and stale resource reports]\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-9016-E002: Documentation for the reports]\n    E001 --> E002\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | Documentation describes the reports that E001 builds; it must reflect what was actually implemented, including the configurable stale-run age and export behavior. |\n\nNo other edges: E001 is the only code epic (no intra-component splits — one\nlogical change, one team, one repo). The Dashboard is already Konflux\nonboarded, so no onboarding epics or Rule 25 build-pipeline ACs apply.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Stale pipeline-run report (configurable age, retained artifacts) |\n| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | (bundled) CSV export shares the reports' data structures and UI surface — not separately schedulable without duplicating them |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Substantive docs authoring; distinct work stream and component |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n  and no NFRs. Team assignments were taken from architecture-context files;\n  epic ACs were derived from the HLR text. Owners should confirm team\n  assignments at planning time.\n- **Scope trap — data accessibility assumption:** the strategy asserts the\n  notebook controller's last-activity timestamps are available to be\n  surfaced. Architecture context says activity is tracked per kernel through\n  Jupyter server API probes and that the Dashboard accesses components via\n  the Kubernetes API only. If the timestamps turn out not to be readable\n  through the console's existing interfaces, a follow-up epic in the\n  `Notebooks` component (surfacing the data on an interface the console can\n  read) would be required. Mitigated as a verification AC on E001; flagged\n  here for human verification during refinement of E001.\n- **No priority inversions detected:** both P1 HLRs map to one P1 epic; P2\n  items are correctly bundled (HLR-3, shared surface) or separated (HLR-4,\n  docs-authoring exception).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\nin-platform.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27145,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac4bbc8f564db54a","agent_id":"a34d19dde9fa24d4c","session_id":"a9a305b9-00c8-468f-a658-3bf7862f04ab","uuid":"d988e360-ffee-42b3-9bea-1b0df226db9d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:13:42.134Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016 into epics"}
