{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e38d075b-68a4-4655-af61-f519b2141c69","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-978000cdcaf690a5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-pejp3j0x/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the console reporting feature for idle and stale resources:\na per-project idle-workbench report and a per-project stale pipeline-run\nreport, each exportable as CSV. Cluster administrators get a single place in\nthe RHOAI web console to see which workbenches are idle (with their last\nactivity, owner, and reserved resources) and which pipeline runs are stale\n(completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts), so\nthey can reclaim capacity with confidence. The data already exists — the\nnotebook controller tracks last-activity timestamps and Kubeflow Pipelines\nretains run completion metadata — this epic surfaces it; no changes to the\nnotebook controller or Kubeflow Pipelines are in scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Per-project idle-workbench report view in the web console showing, per\n  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking), owner, and reserved resources (HLR-1).\n- Per-project stale pipeline-run report view listing completed runs older\n  than a configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from\n  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata (HLR-2). The stale-age threshold is\n  configurable by administrators.\n- CSV export of either report (HLR-3).\n- Data sourcing stays within the console's existing access paths (Kubernetes\n  API and component interfaces); the notebook controller and Kubeflow\n  Pipelines are consumed as-is, not modified.\n- Incidental UI text and in-console guidance that falls out of these views.\n\nOut of scope (per strategy): automated reclamation or deletion of idle\nresources, and cost/chargeback calculations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with workbenches of varying activity, the idle-workbench\n  report lists each workbench with its last activity, owner, and reserved\n  resources, and the last-activity values reconcile with the notebook\n  controller's tracked activity timestamps.\n- Given a project with completed pipeline runs of varying age, the stale\n  pipeline-run report lists completed runs older than the configured age\n  together with their retained artifacts, and the entries reconcile with\n  Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata.\n- The stale-run age threshold can be changed by an administrator and the\n  report reflects the new threshold.\n- Either report can be exported as a CSV file whose rows match the report\n  currently displayed.\n- The sourcing of last-activity and run-metadata data is verified to work\n  through the console's existing interfaces; if a needed field is not\n  reachable, the gap is raised (and resolved as a follow-up in the owning\n  component) rather than silently approximated.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): idle-workbench report — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export — covered by this epic; it shares the\n  reports' data structures and UI surface and is not separately schedulable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29656,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac4bbc8f564db54a","agent_id":"a34d19dde9fa24d4c","session_id":"a9a305b9-00c8-468f-a658-3bf7862f04ab","uuid":"489a57cd-0aed-4bd8-a42f-9d587aa92167","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:13:56.117Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016 into epics"}
