{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7a1485a0daa51d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the console reporting feature for idle and stale resources:\n34\ta per-project idle-workbench report and a per-project stale pipeline-run\n35\treport, each exportable as CSV. Cluster administrators get a single place in\n36\tthe RHOAI web console to see which workbenches are idle (with their last\n37\tactivity, owner, and reserved resources) and which pipeline runs are stale\n38\t(completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts), so\n39\tthey can reclaim capacity with confidence. The data already exists — the\n40\tnotebook controller tracks last-activity timestamps and Kubeflow Pipelines\n41\tretains run completion metadata — this epic surfaces it; no changes to the\n42\tnotebook controller or Kubeflow Pipelines are in scope.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Per-project idle-workbench report view in the web console showing, per\n47\t  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n48\t  tracking), owner, and reserved resources (HLR-1).\n49\t- Per-project stale pipeline-run report view listing completed runs older\n50\t  than a configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from\n51\t  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata (HLR-2). The stale-age threshold is\n52\t  configurable by administrators.\n53\t- CSV export of either report (HLR-3).\n54\t- Data sourcing stays within the console's existing access paths (Kubernetes\n55\t  API and component interfaces); the notebook controller and Kubeflow\n56\t  Pipelines are consumed as-is, not modified.\n57\t- Incidental UI text and in-console guidance that falls out of these views.\n58\t\n59\tOut of scope (per strategy): automated reclamation or deletion of idle\n60\tresources, and cost/chargeback calculations.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given a project with workbenches of varying activity, the idle-workbench\n65\t  report lists each workbench with its last activity, owner, and reserved\n66\t  resources, and the last-activity values reconcile with the notebook\n67\t  controller's tracked activity timestamps.\n68\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs of varying age, the stale\n69\t  pipeline-run report lists completed runs older than the configured age\n70\t  together with their retained artifacts, and the entries reconcile with\n71\t  Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata.\n72\t- The stale-run age threshold can be changed by an administrator and the\n73\t  report reflects the new threshold.\n74\t- Either report can be exported as a CSV file whose rows match the report\n75\t  currently displayed.\n76\t- The sourcing of last-activity and run-metadata data is verified to work\n77\t  through the console's existing interfaces; if a needed field is not\n78\t  reachable, the gap is raised (and resolved as a follow-up in the owning\n79\t  component) rather than silently approximated.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-1 (P1): idle-workbench report — covered by this epic.\n84\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report — covered by this epic.\n85\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export — covered by this epic; it shares the\n86\t  reports' data structures and UI surface and is not separately schedulable.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1dbeac2ed95674f","agent_id":"aa9d08f0c8c5b4765","session_id":"a9a305b9-00c8-468f-a658-3bf7862f04ab","uuid":"8122ae06-24c9-4b18-9ebf-b8518e01c77f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:15:27.696Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7a1485a0daa51d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
